Bashan OS — licensing
=====================

This file covers three separate things, and they are NOT under the same
terms:

  1. The build scripts and configuration in this repository — open source.
  2. The Bashan artwork, logo, wallpapers and audio — NOT open source.
  3. The thousands of programs that make up the operating system — each
     keeps its own licence. See NOTICES.md.

Read all three sections before redistributing anything.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. THE CODE IN THIS REPOSITORY
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

Which licence to choose, in plain words
---------------------------------------

Two licences were considered for the scripts and configuration. The
difference matters only to someone who takes this code and changes it.

MIT
  Anyone may use the code for anything, including in a closed commercial
  product, as long as they keep the copyright notice. They are not required
  to publish their changes. It is short, it is understood everywhere, and it
  creates no obligations for Bashan Tech LLC.

GPL-3.0
  Anyone may use and change the code, but if they distribute a product built
  from it, they must publish their changed source under the GPL as well. It
  keeps improvements in the open. The cost is that it reaches further than
  people expect: it can complicate combining this code with proprietary code
  later, including Bashan Tech LLC's own.

RECOMMENDATION: MIT.

The reasoning: this repository is a recipe for assembling Debian packages,
not the operating system itself. The parts that genuinely matter to software
freedom — the kernel, the desktop, the browser, the office suite — are
already GPL, LGPL and MPL, and nothing here can weaken that. Choosing GPL-3.0
for the recipe would add obligations for Bashan Tech LLC and for anyone
adapting the build, while protecting software that is already protected by
its own authors' licences. MIT gives the recipe away cleanly and keeps the
brand protected separately, in section 2, which is where the real value is.

Note what neither choice does: it does NOT change the licence of the
operating system produced by this build. The ISO contains GPL software and
carries GPL obligations regardless of what this file says. See section 3.

THIS IS NOT LEGAL ADVICE. The owner of Bashan Tech LLC must confirm the
choice. Switching to GPL-3.0 later means replacing the text below; it does
not require changing any other file.

