2. THE BASHAN BRAND ASSETS — ALL RIGHTS RESERVED
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

The following are proprietary to Bashan Tech LLC and are NOT licensed under
the MIT License above:

  - The name "Bashan OS", the name "Bashan Tech LLC", and the Arabic
    wordmark.
  - THE HAND MARK - the "OK hand" - in every size and every derived form.
    This is the Bashan app logo and a Druze community symbol, and Bashan
    Tech LLC is entitled to use it. It is the brand mark of Bashan Tech LLC,
    all rights reserved, and it is NOT covered by the MIT grant in section 1.
    It ships in public builds; that is a decision about distribution, not a
    licence to anyone else. Removing it is what a fork must do.
    Drawing credited to: ________________________  (to be filled in)
  - The wallpapers.
  - The Trash icon artwork.
  - The boot and welcome audio.
  - The Plymouth, GRUB, SDDM and installer branding built from the above.

Copyright (c) 2026 Bashan Tech LLC. All rights reserved.

No permission is granted to copy, modify or redistribute these assets, and
no trademark rights are granted. If you fork this project, you must remove
them and supply your own. The build has a switch for exactly this purpose:
see `PLACEHOLDER_ASSETS` in `config/build.conf`.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------
2b. ASSET INVENTORY — WHAT MUST BE CONFIRMED BEFORE PUBLISHING
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

"Origin" below records only what the repository itself can prove. Where
nothing records where a file came from, it is marked UNCONFIRMED. UNCONFIRMED
does not mean the rights are missing — it means nobody has written down that
they exist, and the owner of Bashan Tech LLC must confirm them in writing
before this is published.

Generated files inherit the status of whatever they were generated from. That
is why one unconfirmed source file puts dozens of files in doubt.

SOURCE ASSETS — the files everything else is built from

CONFIRMED BY THE OWNER — 2026-10-20

| File | Where it came from | Status |
|---|---|---|
| `assets/branding/logo-source.jpg` (716x749) | **Owner-confirmed.** The "OK hand" is the Bashan app logo and a Druze community symbol; Bashan Tech LLC is entitled to use it. Drawing's creator still to be named — see section 2. | Proprietary, all rights reserved. Ships in public builds. |
| `config/bootloaders/isolinux/splash.png`, `config/bootloaders/grub-pc/splash.png` | The hand above, composited over `bashan-ridge`, which `scripts/22-wallpaper.py` draws from code. Both inputs are ours. | Proprietary, all rights reserved. Ships in public builds. |
| Everything generated from the hand: Plymouth logos, the GRUB, SDDM and installer logos, the installer banner, the app icons, `default-face.png`, `logo-ascii.txt` | `scripts/20-bashan-app-icons.py`, `scripts/25-desktop-theme.py`, `scripts/30-boot-branding.py` | Proprietary, all rights reserved. Ship in public builds. |

STILL UNCONFIRMED — the owner must confirm these in writing

| File | Where it came from | Owner must confirm rights? |
|---|---|---|
| `assets/reference/trash-icons.jpg` (1280x640) | Supplied by the owner. Named a "reference", but `scripts/21-trash-icons.py` cuts the shipped Trash icons straight out of it — its own comment says the icons "keep exactly the artwork from the reference". It is source artwork, not a reference. | **YES — UNCONFIRMED** |
| `assets/reference/dock-reference.jpg` (1280x853) | Supplied by the owner. No script reads it; it appears to be a visual reference only and nothing derived from it ships. | **YES — UNCONFIRMED** (but nothing ships from it; deleting it costs nothing) |
| `assets/audio/boot-song.mp3` (103 KB) | Supplied by the owner. No author, title or licence metadata; re-encoded with ffmpeg, which erased anything that may have been there. | **YES — UNCONFIRMED. This is blocker #1.** |
| `branding/boot-song/boot-song.wav` (914 KB) | The same recording as above, converted to WAV for playback. | **YES — same recording, same question** |
| `theme/wallpapers/bashan-mountain-original-1280x1024.png` | Supplied by the owner as an image attachment during Build 16. A photographic image of three people on a mountain. No author or licence recorded. | **YES — UNCONFIRMED. It is the default desktop wallpaper.** |
