SUMMARY: as of 2026-10-20, SIX source files still need the owner's written
confirmation - the two reference images, the two copies of the audio, and the
mountain photograph in its three sizes (counted once). The audio and the
mountain wallpaper, which carries the Arabic wordmark, are the two that stop
a release.

The hand mark came off this list on 2026-10-20 on the owner's confirmation.
It is proprietary to Bashan Tech LLC and excluded from the MIT grant, and it
now ships in public builds. One thing is still missing: the name of whoever
drew it. Section 2 has a line for it.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. THE OPERATING SYSTEM ITSELF
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

Bashan OS is assembled from Debian. The programs in the ISO are not ours and
are not covered by this file. Each carries its own licence and copyright
statement in the running system at:

    /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright

Most are GPL-2.0, GPL-3.0, LGPL, MPL-2.0, Apache-2.0, MIT or BSD. Some
firmware is non-free and redistributable only under its own terms.

The GPL requires that source code be available to everyone who receives the
binaries. See NOTICES.md for the written offer of source code and how to
obtain it.

Nothing in section 1 or section 2 of this file reduces any right that the
GPL, LGPL, MPL or any other licence gives you over the software it covers.
Where this file conflicts with such a licence, that licence wins.
